.TH "EPX\-PRODUCTS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-products \- read, create, update and delete products
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products [flags]
epx products [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes products. Reads find products published and unpublished (without the product.product_read_unpublished scope, Emporix would silently omit unpublished products). create, update and patch change one product, bulk\-create and bulk\-update up to 200, import any number in batches, each from \fB\-\-file\fR; recalculate rebuilds variant trees; delete deletes one.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR. Its writes require the product.product_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx products bulk\-create"
Create products in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products bulk\-create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the products in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of products, each as create takes it. Emporix answers each product with its index, id, code (the HTTP status of the product, e.g. 201) and status (e.g. CREATED), and a message where it failed.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-allow\-publish\fR also requests the product.product_publish scope. Without it, Emporix refuses a product that the write publishes (403 Forbidden, exit 3).
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-publish\fR
Allow the write to publish products, which needs a scope of its own (requests product.product_publish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-do\-index <string>\fR
Whether Emporix reindexes the products it writes (by default, it does; with false, other changes or Emporix\(aqs scheduled indexing may still index them, as it may index a product published with false): true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-related\-items\-validation\fR
Do not check that related products exist, as when they are written later (a tenant may ignore it and refuse unknown related products all the same).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-variant\-generation\fR
Do not generate the variants of a PARENT_VARIANT product from its variant attributes.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx products bulk\-update"
Upsert products in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products bulk\-update [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upserts the products in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of products, each complete and with its id, as update takes it. import sends more than 200 in batches. Emporix answers each product with its index, id, code (the HTTP status of the product, e.g. 201) and status (e.g. CREATED), and a message where it failed.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 200 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
