.SS "epx products delete"
Delete a product.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the product ID. A parent variant product (PARENT_VARIANT, or DYNAMIC_VARIANT with variants below it) is deleted only with \fB\-\-force\fR, with every variant below it (without it, Emporix answers 400 Bad Request, exit 1). An unknown ID is no error: Emporix answers as for a deleted product.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. With \fB\-\-force\fR, it deletes the product and every variant below it with one request. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Delete a parent variant product with every variant below it.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx products get"
Show one product.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads products, published and unpublished (without the product.product_read_unpublished scope, Emporix would silently omit unpublished products).
.PP
Where a mixin\(aqs schema is site\-aware, an item may hold, besides the mixin NAME, an overlay for a site, NAME__SITE, with the values that differ there. \fB\-\-mixin\-site\fR SITE sends SITE as the emporix\-site header: Emporix then merges the overlay of SITE into NAME (nested objects member by member; arrays and other values are replaced, not merged; a null leaves the base value) and leaves out every overlay. A site without an overlay, or one the tenant lacks (codes are case\-sensitive; epx does not check them), gets NAME as stored. Without \fB\-\-mixin\-site\fR, mixins and overlays are read as stored, whatever the default site of the profile. Tables leave mixins (attribute values) out; \fB\-o json\fR and \fB\-o yaml\fR print them, as \fB\-\-stream\fR does on a list.
.PP
A merged item is that site\(aqs view, not the item as stored. Do not write it back with update, bulk\-update or (products) import, which replace whole items and would delete every overlay, nor build a patch from it: NAME would take the site\(aqs values.
.PP
Requires the product.product_read_unpublished scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, CODE, TYPE, PUBLISHED, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-mixin\-site <SITE>\fR
Merge the site\-aware mixin overlays of the site SITE (NAME__SITE) into their mixins.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx products import"
Upsert the products of a file in batches.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products import [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Upserts the products in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of any number of products, each complete and with its id as update takes it, as bulk\-update does up to 200. To resume an import that stopped, send the products from the item that its error names: a product sent again is upserted again, but one whose metadata.version the import changed is a conflict. Emporix answers each product with its index, id, code (the HTTP status of the product, e.g. 201) and status (e.g. CREATED), and a message where it failed.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
epx sends the items in requests of up to 200, in order, confirmed once, and stops at a request that fails as a whole, sending none after it. Emporix carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-allow\-publish\fR also requests the product.product_publish scope. Without it, Emporix refuses a product that the write publishes (403 Forbidden, exit 3). \fB\-\-allow\-unpublish\fR also requests the product.product_unpublish scope. Without it, Emporix refuses a product that the write unpublishes (403 Forbidden, exit 3).
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-publish\fR
Allow the write to publish products, which needs a scope of its own (requests product.product_publish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-unpublish\fR
Allow the write to unpublish products, which needs a scope of its own (requests product.product_unpublish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-do\-index <string>\fR
Whether Emporix reindexes the products it writes (by default, it does; with false, other changes or Emporix\(aqs scheduled indexing may still index them, as it may index a product published with false): true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-related\-items\-validation\fR
Do not check that related products exist, as when they are written later (a tenant may ignore it and refuse unknown related products all the same).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-variant\-generation\fR
Do not generate the variants of a PARENT_VARIANT product from its variant attributes.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx products list"
List products.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads products, published and unpublished (without the product.product_read_unpublished scope, Emporix would silently omit unpublished products).
.PP
Where a mixin\(aqs schema is site\-aware, an item may hold, besides the mixin NAME, an overlay for a site, NAME__SITE, with the values that differ there. \fB\-\-mixin\-site\fR SITE sends SITE as the emporix\-site header: Emporix then merges the overlay of SITE into NAME (nested objects member by member; arrays and other values are replaced, not merged; a null leaves the base value) and leaves out every overlay. A site without an overlay, or one the tenant lacks (codes are case\-sensitive; epx does not check them), gets NAME as stored. Without \fB\-\-mixin\-site\fR, mixins and overlays are read as stored, whatever the default site of the profile. Tables leave mixins (attribute values) out; \fB\-o json\fR and \fB\-o yaml\fR print them, as \fB\-\-stream\fR does on a list.
