.SS "epx products recalculate"
Recalculate the variant trees of dynamic variant products.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products recalculate [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Starts the recalculation of the variant trees of DYNAMIC_VARIANT products once their products are written in bulk (a write of one product updates its tree at once). Emporix finds the root product of each ID, at any level, and starts one job per root, which \fBepx products recalculation\-jobs list\fR shows (jobs). An ID that is unknown, is not of a DYNAMIC_VARIANT product, or whose root has a job pending or processing is skipped (skippedProductIds, left out when none is); where every ID is, the answer has no jobs. Takes up to 1000 IDs, given with \fB\-\-product\fR or in the JSON object of \fB\-\-file\fR (\fB{"productIds": [...]}\fR).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-product <ID>\fR
ID of a product to recalculate (repeatable; required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx products recalculation\-jobs"
Read variant recalculation jobs.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products recalculation\-jobs [flags]
epx products recalculation\-jobs [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the jobs that rebuild the variant tree of a DYNAMIC_VARIANT product once a recalculation was triggered, one per ROOT PRODUCT (an id). STATUS is PENDING, PROCESSING, FINISHED, FAILED or FAILED_PERMANENT, ATTEMPTS counts processing attempts and ERROR says why a job failed; \fB\-o json\fR adds the product ids it was requested for and when processing started, and leaves out each of processingStartedAt, finishedAt and error until it is set. Emporix removes jobs about 30 days after they end. The jobs of one status: \fBepx api get /product/{tenant}/products/recalculate/jobs \-p status=FAILED \-\-scope product.product_manage\fR.
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR.
.SS "epx products recalculation\-jobs get"
Show one recalculation job.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products recalculation\-jobs get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the jobs that rebuild the variant tree of a DYNAMIC_VARIANT product once a recalculation was triggered, one per ROOT PRODUCT (an id). STATUS is PENDING, PROCESSING, FINISHED, FAILED or FAILED_PERMANENT, ATTEMPTS counts processing attempts and ERROR says why a job failed; \fB\-o json\fR adds the product ids it was requested for and when processing started, and leaves out each of processingStartedAt, finishedAt and error until it is set. Emporix removes jobs about 30 days after they end. The jobs of one status: \fBepx api get /product/{tenant}/products/recalculate/jobs \-p status=FAILED \-\-scope product.product_manage\fR.
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR
Opt in to requesting product.product_manage, which can also change data (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ROOT PRODUCT, STATUS, ATTEMPTS, CREATED, FINISHED, ERROR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx products recalculation\-jobs list"
List variant recalculation jobs.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products recalculation\-jobs list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the jobs that rebuild the variant tree of a DYNAMIC_VARIANT product once a recalculation was triggered, one per ROOT PRODUCT (an id). STATUS is PENDING, PROCESSING, FINISHED, FAILED or FAILED_PERMANENT, ATTEMPTS counts processing attempts and ERROR says why a job failed; \fB\-o json\fR adds the product ids it was requested for and when processing started, and leaves out each of processingStartedAt, finishedAt and error until it is set. Emporix removes jobs about 30 days after they end. The jobs of one status: \fBepx api get /product/{tenant}/products/recalculate/jobs \-p status=FAILED \-\-scope product.product_manage\fR.
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope. Opt\-in: epx requests a write\-capable scope for a read only when given \fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-write\-scope\fR
Opt in to requesting product.product_manage, which can also change data (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, ROOT PRODUCT, STATUS, ATTEMPTS, CREATED, FINISHED, ERROR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx products search"
Search products.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the products, published and unpublished, that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every product). It reads and shows them as \fBepx products list\fR does.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Where a mixin\(aqs schema is site\-aware, an item may hold, besides the mixin NAME, an overlay for a site, NAME__SITE, with the values that differ there. \fB\-\-mixin\-site\fR SITE sends SITE as the emporix\-site header: Emporix then merges the overlay of SITE into NAME (nested objects member by member; arrays and other values are replaced, not merged; a null leaves the base value) and leaves out every overlay. A site without an overlay, or one the tenant lacks (codes are case\-sensitive; epx does not check them), gets NAME as stored. Without \fB\-\-mixin\-site\fR, mixins and overlays are read as stored, whatever the default site of the profile. Tables leave mixins (attribute values) out; \fB\-o json\fR and \fB\-o yaml\fR print them, as \fB\-\-stream\fR does on a list.
.PP
A merged item is that site\(aqs view, not the item as stored. Do not write it back with update, bulk\-update or (products) import, which replace whole items and would delete every overlay, nor build a patch from it: NAME would take the site\(aqs values.
.PP
Requires the product.product_read_unpublished scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, CODE, TYPE, PUBLISHED, NAME.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-mixin\-site <SITE>\fR
Merge the site\-aware mixin overlays of the site SITE (NAME__SITE) into their mixins.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx products update"
Upsert a product.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx products update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces product ID with the JSON object of \fB\-\-file\fR, the complete product: an upsert, as Emporix creates the product where none has the ID (and answers with its id and yrn). Mixins left out are removed. Emporix refuses it as a conflict (exit 5) when another product has its code or, given metadata.version, when the product changed since that version.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
\fB\-\-allow\-publish\fR also requests the product.product_publish scope. Without it, Emporix refuses a product that the write publishes (403 Forbidden, exit 3). \fB\-\-allow\-unpublish\fR also requests the product.product_unpublish scope. Without it, Emporix refuses a product that the write unpublishes (403 Forbidden, exit 3).
.PP
Requires the product.product_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-publish\fR
Allow the write to publish products, which needs a scope of its own (requests product.product_publish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-unpublish\fR
Allow the write to unpublish products, which needs a scope of its own (requests product.product_unpublish too).
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-do\-index <string>\fR
Whether Emporix reindexes the products it writes (by default, it does; with false, other changes or Emporix\(aqs scheduled indexing may still index them, as it may index a product published with false): true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-related\-items\-validation\fR
Do not check that related products exist, as when they are written later (a tenant may ignore it and refuse unknown related products all the same).
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-variant\-generation\fR
Do not generate the variants of a PARENT_VARIANT product from its variant attributes.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
